<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.8.3: Using Function Language and Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01389</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.8.3: Using Function Language and Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>65f28687-6f62-4c88-8d5c-d75c0cd03816</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">An exponential function is written in the form \(f(x)=ab^x\), where \(a\) is the initial value and \(b\) is the growth factor.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00002"> In a biology lab, a population of 50 bacteria reproduce by splitting. Every hour, on the hour, each bacterium splits into two bacteria.</para>
      
      <para id="para-00003"> Write a sentence of the form “_____ is a function of _____.”</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    <para id="para-00004"/>
  
  <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00006"> The number of bacteria is a function of time passed in hours.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    
    
    <para id="para-00007"> Indicate which is the independent and which is the dependent variable.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    <para id="para-00008"/>
  
  <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00010"> Independent: number of hours. Dependent: number of bacteria.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    
    
    <para id="para-00011"> Write an equation that represents the situation using function notation.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
    
    <para id="para-00012"/>
  
  <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00014">\(
      f(t)=50 \cdot 2^t\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00004">
  <problem id="prob-00004">
    <para id="para-00015"> Every year after a new car is purchased, it loses \(\frac13\) of its value. Let’s say that the new car costs $18,000.</para>
      
      <para id="para-00016"> Write a sentence of the form “_____ is a function of _____.”</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00004">
    
    <para id="para-00017"/>
  
  <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00019"> The value of a car is a function of the number of years since purchase.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00005">
  <problem id="prob-00005">
    
    
    <para id="para-00020"> Indicate which is the independent and which is the dependent variable.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00005">
    
    <para id="para-00021"/>
  
  <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00023"> Independent: number of years since purchase of car. Dependent: value of car in dollars.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00006">
  <problem id="prob-00006">
    
    
    <para id="para-00024"> Write an equation that represents the situation using function notation.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00006">
    
    <para id="para-00025"/>
  
  <para id="para-00026">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00027">\(
      f(t)=18,000 \cdot (\frac{2}{3})^t\). Note: \(\frac13\) is the rate, and growth factor \(=1-\) rate, so the growth factor is \(\frac23\) because there’s \(\frac23\) left.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00007">
  <problem id="prob-00007">
    <para id="para-00028">To control an algae bloom in a lake, scientists introduce some treatment products. The day they begin treatment, the area covered by algae is 240 square yards. Each day since the treatment began, a third of the previous day’s area (in square yards) remains covered by algae. Time \(t\) is measured in days.</para>
      
      <para id="para-00029"> Write a sentence of the form “_____ is a function of _____.”</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00007">
    
    <para id="para-00030"/>
  
  <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00032"> The area covered by algae is a function of the number of days since the treatment.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00008">
  <problem id="prob-00008">
    
    
    <para id="para-00033"> Indicate which is the independent and which is the dependent variable.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00008">
    
    <para id="para-00034"/>
  
  <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00036">Independent: number of days since treatment. Dependent: area of algae in square yards.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00009">
  <problem id="prob-00009">
    
    
    <para id="para-00037"> Write an equation that represents the situation using function notation.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00009">
    
    <para id="para-00038"/>
  
  <para id="para-00039">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00040">\(
      f(t)=240 \cdot (\frac{1}{3})^t\). Note: \(\frac13\) is given as the growth factor because it represents what remains.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise></section>
<!--Interaction End -->
<section id="sect-00002">
<title>Video: Writing an Exponential Function from a Situation</title>
<para id="para-00041">Watch the following video to learn more about exponential functions:</para>
<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f2d45c545d1156f3892ee978458e09e568332b09"/></media></section>
<note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
  <para id="para-00042">A new computer is purchased for $2,500. Each year after its purchase, it loses \(\frac15\) of its value. Which equation represents this situation?</para>
</note>
<section id="sect-00003">
  <title>Additional Resources</title>
  
  <section id="sect-00004"><title> Writing Functions from Exponential Situations</title>

    <note id="note-00002">
      <title> EXPONENTIAL GROWTH </title>
      <para id="para-00043">A function that models exponential growth grows by a rate proportional to the amount present. For any real number
        \(x\) and any positive real numbers \(a\) and \(b\) such that \(b \neq 1\), an exponential growth function has
        the form</para>
      <para id="para-00044">\(f(x)=ab^x\)</para>
      <para id="para-00045">where</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>\(a\) is the initial or starting value of the function.</item>
        <item>\(b\) is the growth factor or growth multiplier per unit \(x\).</item>
      </list>
    </note>
    
    <para><emphasis id="para-00046">Example 1</emphasis></para>
    <para id="para-00047">The starting value of the function is 10.   This function doubles every year.</para>
    <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis>Growth factor function</emphasis></entry><entry>\(𝑓(𝑥)=𝑎b^x\)</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>Identify the initial value.</emphasis></entry><entry>\(a = 10\)</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>Identify the growth factor.</emphasis></entry><entry>\(b = 2\)</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>Identify the unit.</emphasis></entry><entry>\(x = t\) for time in years.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>Write the exponential equation.</emphasis></entry><entry>\(𝑓(y)=10 \cdot 2^t\)</entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    <para><emphasis id="para-00048">Example 2</emphasis></para>
    <para id="para-00049">An acre of land is worth $40,000 at the time of purchase. It doubles in value every decade. Write an equation for
      this situation where \(t\) is time in decades.</para>
    <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis>Identify the initial value.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(a=40,000\) </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>Identify the growth factor.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(b=2\) </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>Write the exponential equation.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(f(t)=40,000 \cdot 2^t\) </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    
    <note class="try" id="note-00003">
    <title>Try It: Writing Functions from Exponential Situations</title>
    
    <!--Q#1-->
    <exercise id="exer-00010">
      <problem id="prob-00010">
        
        <para id="para-00050">The starting value of the function is 150.   This function triples every decade</para>
        <para id="para-00051">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
      
      </problem><solution id="sol-00010">
      <para id="para-00052">Compare your answer:</para>
      
      <para id="para-00053">Here is how to write an exponential function from a situation:</para>
      
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00003">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>Identify the initial value.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(a=150\) </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Identify the growth factor.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(b=3\) </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Write the exponential equation.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(f(y)=150 \cdot 3^t\) </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    </solution></exercise>
    <!--Interaction End --> 
    
    <exercise id="exer-00011">
      <problem id="prob-00011">
        
        <para id="para-00054">When first measured, the population of deer in a forest is 40. Over time, the population triples every year.
            Write an exponential equation where \(t\) is time in years.</para>
        <para id="para-00055">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
      
      </problem><solution id="sol-00011">
      <para id="para-00056">Compare your answer:</para>
      
      <para id="para-00057">Here is how to write an exponential function from a situation:</para>
      
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00004">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>Identify the initial value.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(a=40\) </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Identify the growth factor.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(b=3\) </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Write the exponential equation.</emphasis></entry><entry> \(f(t)=40 \cdot 3^t\) </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    </solution></exercise></note>
    </section>
</section>

